# Where the 206 bones are
subtitle: "A tour of the adult skeleton that tallies its 206 bones region by region, and shows why more than half sit in the hands and feet."
tags: ["anatomy","skeleton","human body","bones","hands and feet"]
teaches: ["anatomy/skeletal-regions","anatomy/bone-count","anatomy/skeletal-structure"]
thumb: "card wood"
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achernar | a soft, clear anatomy guide; calm, never sleepy","take":"lines"}

## Where the 206 bones are
use: anatomy
with:
    systems:
      - skeleton
    detail: 3
    color: mono
    outline: line
    labels: none
    box:
      x: 40
      'y': 150
      w: 920
      h: 530

    text t_axial "Axial  80" x 250 y 540 font_size 36 hidden true
    text t_arms "Arms  64" x 250 y 470 font_size 36 hidden true
    text t_legs "Legs  62" x 250 y 400 font_size 36 hidden true
    text t_total "= 206" #2f6b8f x 260 y 320 font_size 40 hidden true
    text l_sternum "sternum →" #2f6b8f x 345 y 545 font_size 30 hidden true
    text c_wrist "8 wrist" #2f6b8f x 625 y 417 font_size 16 hidden true
    text c_palm "5 palm" #2f6b8f x 625 y 395 font_size 16 hidden true
    text c_fing "14 fingers" #2f6b8f x 632 y 373 font_size 16 hidden true
    text c_foot "26 each" #2f6b8f x 625 y 190 font_size 34 hidden true

    card title "Where the 206 bones are"

    hide shoulder_left shoulder_right elbow_left elbow_right wrist_left wrist_right hip_left hip_right knee_left knee_right ankle_left ankle_right jaw

Where in your body are the 206 bones of an adult skeleton? Start at the top: the skull, with the lower jaw hinged beneath it.
    draw body_outline cranium mandible

Down the middle runs the spine: seven neck vertebrae, twelve in the chest, five in the lower back, then the sacrum.
    draw cervical_vertebrae thoracic_vertebrae lumbar_vertebrae sacrum

From the chest vertebrae hang twelve pairs of ribs, and most of them meet in front at the breastbone, the sternum.
    draw ribs sternum l_sternum

That central column, plus a few small bones in the ears and throat, is the axial skeleton: eighty bones that protect the brain, the spinal cord and the heart.
    highlight cranium mandible cervical_vertebrae thoracic_vertebrae lumbar_vertebrae sacrum ribs sternum

    erase l_sternum

Keep a tally: eighty so far. Everything else hangs from this column.
    draw t_axial

The arms hang from a ring of four bones: two collarbones in front, two shoulder blades behind.
    draw clavicle_left clavicle_right scapula_left scapula_right

Below that, one bone in the upper arm, then two in the forearm, so the forearm can twist.
    draw humerus_left humerus_right radius_left ulna_left radius_right ulna_right

The legs hang from the pelvis in the same pattern: one thigh bone, then two in the lower leg, plus the kneecap.
    draw hip_bones femur_left femur_right patella_left patella_right tibia_left fibula_left tibia_right fibula_right

    pause 0.4

Now the hands, where the count climbs fast: each one holds 27 bones.
    draw carpals_left metacarpals_left phalanges_hand_left carpals_right metacarpals_right phalanges_hand_right

    camera on ["carpals_left","metacarpals_left","phalanges_hand_left","c_wrist","c_palm","c_fing","radius_left"] zoom fit duration 1.2

Eight in the wrist, five in the palm, and fourteen in the fingers.
    draw c_wrist c_palm c_fing

    erase c_wrist c_palm c_fing parallel true

    camera reset true duration 1.2

So the arms and shoulders together come to sixty-four.
    draw t_arms

Each foot holds 26, built on the same plan, so the hips and legs come to sixty-two.
    draw tarsals_left metatarsals_left phalanges_foot_left tarsals_right metatarsals_right phalanges_foot_right c_foot t_legs

Eighty, sixty-four and sixty-two make 206.
    draw t_total

A newborn starts with around 300; many fuse as it grows. This sacrum began as five separate vertebrae.
    focus sacrum

    erase c_foot

    ask "Click on the bone where the ribs meet in front." widget click answer sternum
        right: The sternum, the breastbone: the upper ribs join it through cartilage.

    quiz "Roughly what share of the 206 bones sit in the hands and feet?"
        right: More than half: 27 in each hand and 26 in each foot make 106 of the 206.
        * About a tenth
        * About a quarter
        + More than half

